# .easignore — what NOT to upload to EAS Build.
#
# ⚠️ This file REPLACES .gitignore for the build archive; eas-cli stops reading
# .gitignore entirely once this exists. So every dependency and build-output
# rule has to be re-listed here, or the archive gets BIGGER, not smaller.
#
# Why it exists: the archive is the whole git repo, not apps/mobile — that is
# what lets packages/shared reach the builders (see apps/mobile/metro.config.js).
# But it also meant web/.next, 991 MB of stale Next.js output, uploaded on every
# iOS build. web/.gitignore ignores it; eas-cli does not honour that nested
# ignore file from the mobile project root. Measured 2026-08-29: 1,025 MB.
#
# Verify any change to this file for free, without spending a build:
#   npx eas-cli build:inspect -p ios -s archive -e preview -o <dir> --force
#
# Keep apps/mobile/** and packages/shared/** — the build needs both.
#
# There is a SECOND .easignore at apps/mobile/.easignore. It is not redundant:
# it scopes the project directory, this one scopes the repo around it. Both
# apply, gitignore-style. Measured after this file: 22 MB.

# --- dependencies and build output (re-listed: .gitignore is not read) ---
node_modules/
.expo/
dist/
web-build/
.next/
*.tsbuildinfo
.metro-health-check*

# --- the web app: 991 MB of .next, and nothing an iOS build needs ---
web/

# --- deleted in the alignment work; the directory lingers ---
frontend/

# --- repo material a mobile build never reads ---
docs/
tests/
test_reports/
supabase/
memory/
scripts/
skills-lock.json
design_guidelines.json
design-lab-preview.png
/*.md
.github/
.claude/

# --- credentials and local env never belong in an upload ---
.env
.env.*
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.mobileprovision
*.pem
